Additional permission under AGPLv3 section 7:

You are not required to include configuration include files (such as
config.inc, or similar files containing deployment-specific
constants) in the Corresponding Source that you provide under section 13,
provided that:

1. These files contain only deployment-specific parameters (e.g., TCP
   ports, file paths, hostnames, credentials, boolean feature toggles)
   and do not introduce new program logic, algorithms, or control-flow
   modifications beyond what those parameters control;
2. A template or example version of such file (e.g., config.inc.example)
   is included in the Corresponding Source so that recipients can still
   build the Program.
